{
  "category": "Water Gun Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "They knock down flying prey by firing compressed water from their massive claws like shooting a pistol.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Through controlled explosions of internal gas, it can expel water like a pistol shot. At close distances, it can shatter rock.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "They knock down flying prey by firing compressed water from their massive claws like shooting a pistol.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Through controlled explosions of internal gas, it can expel water like a pistol shot. At close distances, it can shatter rock.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its claws occasionally fall off, and it keeps a low profile until they grow back. The meat of its claws is so delicious!",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It moves around by jetting water from its right pincer. It has a poor sense of balance, so it’s terrible at swimming straight.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Clauncher’s claws can fall off during battle, but they’ll regenerate. The meat inside the claws is popular as a delicacy in Galar.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "By detonating gas that accumulates in its right claw, this Pokémon launches water like a bullet. This is how Clauncher defeats its enemies.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
